ellaneous clippings.</unittitle><container id="aspace_a1a774c370af99e8456a74d2c65c3fe7" label="Mixed Materials" type="box">3</container><container id="aspace_ca87fcc9b5e717e7d6fea47bf00f2268" parent="aspace_a1a774c370af99e8456a74d2c65c3fe7" type="folder">11</container></did><odd id="aspace_ce8af75e522bedffb30e3fc1e9737ad1"><head>General note</head><p>Additional materials donated March 1985.</p></odd></c02></c01><c01 id="aspace_ref60_bof" level="series"><did><unittitle>Gene Mailes IATSE proceedings oral history recordings and related materials.</unittitle><physdesc altrender="whole"><extent altrender="materialtype spaceoccupied">0.4 linear feet</extent><extent altrender="carrier">(1 document box)</extent></physdesc><physdesc altrender="part"><extent altrender="materialtype spaceoccupied">5 audiovisual carriers</extent><extent altrender="carrier">(5 audiocassettes)</extent></physdesc><unitdate datechar="creation">ca. 1945-1985.</unitdate><container id="aspace_d697f59125a6e1bdda4a0a708aee069d" label="Mixed Materials" type="box">4</container></did><scopecontent id="aspace_83991b82538abcddb9aba47c840a923f"><head>Scope and Contents</head><p>Cassette tape recordings of Gene Mailes' reminiscences relating to the IATSE proceedings and related copy proceedings and printed materials.</p></scopecontent><phystech id="aspace_9731bd4f5ea391322e5f2122f5f91b9a"><head>Physical Characteristics and Technical Requirements</head><p>CONTAINS UNPROCESSED AUDIO MATERIALS: Audio materials are not currently available for access and will require further processing and assessment. If you have questions about this material please email AskLSC@library.ucla.edu.</p></phystech></c01><c01 id="aspace_ec30c1c35381b2550230f287a5d3e7ca" level="series"><did><unittitle>Accession LSC-1999-004 backlog material</unittitle><unitid>LSC-1999-004</unitid><physdesc altrender="whole"><extent altrender="materialtype spaceoccupied">1.5 linear feet</extent><extent altrender="carrier">(1 flat box)</extent></physdesc><container altrender="flat box (11.75d 3h 17.75w)" id="aspace_927b8751deb348484a6ba46fdcb54ef9" label="Mixed Materials" type="box">5</container></did><accessrestrict id="aspace_50de613ffe72ca4be97a970af834319b"><head>Conditions Governing Access</head><p>Unprocessed series. This material is unavailable for access. Please see <extref xlink:actuate="onRequest" xlink:show="new" xlink:href="https://www.library.ucla.edu/location/library-special-collections/discover-collections/access-unprocessed-collections-policy">LSC's Access to Unprocessed Collections Policy</extref> for more information about levels of discovery and access of special collections materials and registering interest in unprocessed collections.</p></accessrestrict><scopecontent id="aspace_0b0891c643f1db3c658ec6a2b70dd0ff"><head>Scope and Contents</head><p>Addition to the Hollywood Studios strike collection (LSC-0226). Materials consist of news publications, pamphlets, telegrams and magazines, primarily from the point of view of the striking workers. Includes publications in support of the strike like CSU News produced by the Conference of Studio Unions (CSU) and the Hollywood Atom by the 15 local unions belonging to the Hollywood Studio Strike Strategy Committee.</p></scopecontent></c01></dsc>
